What:		/dev/goodix_fp
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	zuwwik <zuwwiks@gmail.com>
Description:
		Normal-world power, reset and IRQ resources of a TEE-managed
		Goodix fingerprint sensor. No images or templates pass through
		this device. The trusted application is accessed separately
		through the platform's TEE interface.

		Opening the device holds the supply and is exclusive. Closing
		it disables interrupts, asserts reset and releases the supply.
		The ioctls in <linux/goodix-fingerprint.h> pulse reset or enable
		and disable interrupt delivery. Reset also disables delivery.

		A blocking read waits for interrupts and returns one
		struct goodix_fp_event containing their accumulated count.
		The reserved field is zero. Reads require a buffer at least
		as large as that structure. With O_NONBLOCK, an empty queue
		returns EAGAIN. poll() reports readable data or device removal.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/.../firmware_name
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	zuwwik <zuwwiks@gmail.com>
Description:
		Read-only trusted application name from firmware-name in the
		device tree. This identifies the board pairing; it does not
		claim protocol compatibility with any other Goodix sensor.
